# ============================================================================
# dsh-web-search-brave — .gitignore
#
# This repository is public. The secret section below is a security control,
# not a formality: if a credential ever lands in the working tree it must not
# be committable. See SECURITY.md.
# ============================================================================

# --- Secrets: never commit a credential -------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret
credentials.json
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.dsh/

# --- Dependencies and package-manager stores --------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/cache/
.yarn/install-state.gz
jspm_packages/

# --- Logs (a log line is a leak vector; none of these are ever committed) ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# --- Test and coverage output -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
*.lcov

# --- Tool output that is never source ----------------------------------------
# A diagnostic tool's working directory: a generated report plus the scratch
# copies a remediation pass makes. Useful on disk, never committed.
.code-dr/
.scratch/

# Linked worktrees. `git worktree add` puts a whole second checkout here, so a
# single un-ignored entry would add every file of it to `git status` — and to the
# credential scan, which reads exactly what `git add -A` would publish.
.worktrees/

# --- Runtime junk ------------------------------------------------------------
*.pid
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/
.npm-cache/
.dts-check/
dist/
build/
out/
tmp/

# --- Editors and operating systems ------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored — these are shipped and must be committed:
#   lib/                 hand-authored ESM source and hand-authored .d.ts.
#                        lib/ is SOURCE, not build output: this package has no
#                        build step, so it is versioned like any other source.
#   test/                the node:test suite (test/helpers/ included)
#   *.md                 README.md, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md
#   package-lock.json    the lockfile is committed on purpose so an install is
#                        reproducible; do not add it to this file.
#   .env.example         placeholder names only, never a real value
#   tsconfig.json        the no-emit config behind `npm run check:types:tsc`;
#                        nothing is ever emitted, so no build output can leak
#   .github/             the CI workflow and the Dependabot config
# ============================================================================
